JotBox Implementation Plan
Executive Summary
Timeline: 6-8 weeks
Team: Solo developer
Platforms: Web (React) + Mobile (React Native/Expo) - monorepo
Architecture: Hybrid AI (Whisper self-hosted for transcription, OpenAI/Gemini APIs for generation)
Backend: Supabase (Auth, PostgreSQL, Edge Functions, Storage)
File Storage: Amazon S3 (signed URLs via Supabase Edge Functions)

Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)
1.1 Monorepo Setup
jotbox/
├── apps/
│   ├── mobile/          # Expo React Native
│   └── web/             # React + Vite + Tailwind
├── packages/
│   ├── ui/              # Shared components (React Native Web compatible)
│   ├── api/             # Shared API client, types
│   ├── ai/              # Shared AI prompts, utilities
│   └── config/          # Shared constants, theme, env
├── supabase/            # Migrations, Edge Functions, seed
└── package.json         # Root workspace (npm/yarn workspaces)
Tools: Turborepo or Nx for build orchestration, TypeScript strict mode throughout

1.2 Supabase Schema
-- Core tables
users (id, email, name, university, course, subscription_type, created_at)
lectures (id, user_id, title, audio_url, duration, status, created_at)
transcripts (id, lecture_id, content, language, created_at)
notes (id, lecture_id, type, content, created_at)  -- type: summary|detailed|revision
flashcards (id, lecture_id, question, answer, difficulty, created_at)
quizzes (id, lecture_id, question, options, answer, type, difficulty, created_at)

-- RLS policies on all tables (user_id = auth.uid())
1.3 Authentication Flow
Supabase Auth (email/password + OAuth: Google, Apple)
Shared auth context across web/mobile
Protected routes, session persistence
Phase 2: Core Recording & Transcription (Week 2-3)
2.1 Mobile Recording
Expo Audio (expo-audio) for recording with pause/resume
Waveform visualization (react-native-skia or reanimated)
Background recording support
Upload to S3 via presigned URL from Edge Function
2.2 Transcription Pipeline (Edge Function)
POST /functions/v1/transcribe
  Body: { lectureId, audioUrl }
  → Download audio from S3
  → Whisper.cpp (self-hosted on Railway/Render/Fly.io) or OpenAI Whisper API
  → Store transcript in DB
  → Trigger notes generation
Hybrid approach: Start with OpenAI Whisper API (faster dev), migrate to self-hosted Whisper.cpp for cost optimization later.

Phase 3: AI Generation Pipeline (Week 3-4)
3.1 Notes Generation (Edge Function)
POST /functions/v1/generate-notes
  Body: { lectureId, transcript, types: ['summary', 'detailed', 'revision'] }
  → Single LLM call with structured output (JSON schema)
  → Store each note type in notes table
Prompt strategy: One comprehensive prompt → structured JSON → parse into 3 note types

3.2 Flashcards & Quizzes (Edge Functions)
POST /functions/v1/generate-flashcards
POST /functions/v1/generate-quizzes
Batch generation (10-20 cards/questions per lecture)
Difficulty distribution: 40% easy, 40% medium, 20% hard
Store with lecture_id for retrieval
AI Provider: OpenAI GPT-4o-mini (cost-effective) with Gemini fallback

